      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CATIES SON (2) was in the money at Shepparton two runs ago before making up plenty of ground but finding a couple better at his latest appearance over 2180m at this track. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Good enough to put himself in the winners' stall. NINEDOLLA TOASTIE (1) resumes from a spell of ten weeks after closing off last campaign in good form, the last run being a solid third over 1720m at Melton. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Likely to run a big race to kick off this campaign. GIVE FRED A CLAP (9) finished seventh two runs ago then broke and finished a distant fourth over 1720m at Melton at the latest appearance. This doesn't look as hard so he is capable of turning things around. EAGLE MAJOR (5) is in the mix following a respectable third at his most recent appearance over 1740m at Riverina Paceway.",
